-- =====================================================================
-- RRNetBanking — Slice 7 (Open an additional account)
--
-- Legacy: newregistration.jsp + PDAO.reg().
--
-- A DELIBERATE DEPARTURE, stated here because it is the largest one in
-- the project.
--
-- The legacy page collected a NEW LOGIN ID and password, and reg()
-- inserted a whole new customer identity — custp (login), cust (account
-- to login), custd (name, address, mobile copied from the session's
-- customer) and accd (the account). So "open a second account" actually
-- meant "create a second customer who happens to have your details",
-- because the legacy schema tied one login to one account through
-- cust(cac, cid).
--
-- Slice 1 replaced that with Customer 1..* Account. Reproducing the
-- legacy behaviour on top of it would duplicate every customer's personal
-- details once per account — the same data smeared across rows that KYC
-- rules exist to prevent, and a second set of credentials for the
-- customer to manage. So this opens an account UNDER THE EXISTING LOGIN.
--
-- What is kept: the entry point ("through his previous account"), the
-- branch, and the zero opening balance. What is dropped: the new login.
--
-- The legacy number-allocation defect goes with it. newregistration.jsp
-- read the next number with `select * from acc`, showed it in a disabled
-- input AND a hidden field named `acn`, and reg() trusted that hidden
-- field before running `update acc set cac=cac+1`. Two customers opening
-- an account at the same time got the same number, and anyone could edit
-- the hidden field. AutoNumber assigns the number at commit; the form
-- below has no account-number field at all.
-- =====================================================================

/**
 * Form state for opening an account. The only choice the customer makes
 * is the branch — the number is the bank's to assign.
 */
CREATE OR MODIFY NON-PERSISTENT ENTITY Banking.OpenAccountForm (
  Acknowledged: Boolean
)
COMMENT 'Form state for opening an additional account. Not stored.';
/

CREATE OR MODIFY ASSOCIATION Banking.OpenAccountForm_Branch
  FROM Banking.OpenAccountForm TO Banking.Branch
  TYPE Reference
  COMMENT 'Branch the new account will be held at.';
/
